## Design — Part 1 of 3: Core (data model, catalog, resolver)

**Data model.** Add a single optional field to `ProjectFileGroup`:
```kotlin
data class ProjectFileGroup(
    var groupName: String = "",
    var patterns: MutableList<String> = mutableListOf(),
    var iconKey: String? = null   // NEW. null = use auto-detection
)
```
`XmlSerializerUtil.copyBean` handles this transparently — older `androidViewSettings.xml` files just don't have the field, default `null` preserves current behavior. No migration code needed.

**Icon catalog.** A new singleton `GroupIconCatalog` in `utils/` (or `nodes/`) holds an immutable list of curated entries:
```kotlin
data class GroupIconEntry(val key: String, val displayName: String, val icon: Icon)

object GroupIconCatalog {
    val entries: List<GroupIconEntry> = listOf(
        GroupIconEntry("nodes.module",       "Module",       AllIcons.Nodes.Module),
        GroupIconEntry("general.settings",   "Settings",     AllIcons.General.Settings),
        GroupIconEntry("nodes.dataSchema",   "Database",     AllIcons.Nodes.DataSchema),
        // … ~40 total
    )
    fun find(key: String?): GroupIconEntry? = key?.let { k -> entries.firstOrNull { it.key == k } }
}
```
Stable `key` strings mean we never serialize an Icon — we look it up at render time. If a future IDE renames or removes an `AllIcons` member and the lookup fails, `find` returns null and the resolver falls back gracefully. The 40 chosen icons cover what real users want for these groups: Cloud, Database, Lock/Security, Settings, Tools/Build, Test, Module, Package, Folder variants, Documentation, Bookmarks, Star, Warning, License, Plugin, Web, Console, Terminal, etc. Final list goes in the spec.

**Resolver.** `ProjectFileGroupNode.getGroupIcon()` becomes:
```kotlin
private fun getGroupIcon(): Icon =
    GroupIconCatalog.find(fileGroup.iconKey)?.icon ?: autoDetectIcon()

private fun autoDetectIcon(): Icon { /* current logic, unchanged */ }
```
Override wins when set and resolvable; otherwise the existing auto-detection runs. Existing groups, stale keys, and never-set keys all behave identically (auto-detect).

